@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy & demo terms";
}
<main class="page-shell privacy-page">
    <section class="page-container section-block">
        <span class="section-kicker">A CLEAR NOTE BEFORE YOU EXPLORE</span>
        <h1>Privacy &amp; <span>demo terms.</span></h1>
        <p class="section-subtitle">Evently is a frontend-only demonstration. This page explains what the sample
            interface does and does not do.</p>
            <div class="privacy-grid">
                <article class="panel-card privacy-card" id="privacy">
                    <span class="demo-badge">BROWSER-LOCAL DEMO</span>
                    <h2>Privacy in this demo</h2>
                    <p>Favorites, simulated bookings, attendee details typed into checkout, profile edits, organizer
                        drafts/listings, and admin review changes are saved in this browser’s local storage so the demo can
                        show them on later visits.</p>
                        <p>Please use fictional details rather than real contact information. Nothing in the booking flow
                            reserves a real ticket, sends an email, or processes a payment. Password fields are temporary and
                            are never saved. Payment choices are labels only; the demo never asks for card, bank, GCash, or Maya
                            credentials.</p>
                            <p>Use <strong>Reset demo data</strong> in the Admin demo to clear Evently’s saved sample state from
                                this browser, or clear this site’s local storage in your browser settings. This page describes the
                                Evently frontend only; the hosting service may have separate operational privacy notices.</p>
                            </article>
                            <article class="panel-card privacy-card" id="terms">
                                <span class="demo-badge">ILLUSTRATIVE CONTENT</span>
                                <h2>Demo terms</h2>
                                <p>Event titles, dates, schedules, organizers, venues, addresses, prices, availability, attendee counts,
                                    revenue, testimonials, accounts, and reports are fictional or illustrative sample data. Recurring
                                    festivals are not verified editions, and no listing is a confirmed upcoming event.</p>
                                    <p>Demo tickets and booking references are generated only for interface testing and are not valid for
                                        entry, resale, reimbursement, or payment. Organizer and admin actions affect only local demo state;
                                        they do not publish events, contact people, or change real accounts.</p>
                                        <p>Use the Explore and checkout screens to try the experience, but do not rely on this demo for event
                                            planning or real-world transactions.</p>
                                        </article>
                                    </div>
                                    <a class="button button-outline" href="/">Back to Evently</a>
                                </section>
                            </main>
